What the Results Actually Mean
The Confidence Scores (~0.99) Are Misleading
Every single prediction has a score of 0.96–0.9997. This is expected and normal — Moment-DETR and CG-DETR were trained on QVHighlights, and their sigmoid outputs are not well-calibrated for out-of-distribution videos like yours. A score of 0.99 does NOT mean "the model is 99% sure". It just means the model committed to a region. The IoU against annotations is the real quality indicator.

Video-by-Video Breakdown
Video_21 — Biggest Problem
This is the hardest video (10 min, 24 VLM events). The VLM hallucinated the content — it described events like "A group gathers around inside someone's house for dinner time" and "Two people standing outside their homes during dusk". The real video is a David Belle parkour documentary. These hallucinated descriptions then misguided the moment retrieval models.

Despite this, some events accidentally hit good IoU:

GT "movie clip with tricks" (6:23–6:47) → IoU 0.91 (Moment-DETR) — got lucky, region was covered
GT "TV channel interview" (5:24–5:43) → IoU 0.84 (Moment-DETR)
But the first 3 minutes are completely missed by CG-DETR (all 24 CG-DETR predictions land between 3:37–10:47).

Video_22 — Best Performance
CG-DETR 0.4164 is the best single-video score. Two near-perfect hits:

"Participant speaks and demonstrates jump" (2:41–3:05) → IoU 0.9538
"Coordinated jumps on wall" (3:05–3:40) → IoU 0.9086
Main miss: the 2-minute interview segment (0:21–2:30) gets IoU 0.0 from both models. The VLM only detected 6 events and didn't cover this long continuous region.

Video_23 — Worst Performance (both models ~0.15)
This is a structured narrative video (man's morning commute, ends with parkour). The first 59 seconds contain 4 key events — all 6 VLM-detected events land in the 57–187s range, so the model never even queries for the early events. Root cause: the VLM described escalators, staircases and parking lots — things that appear late in the video — and completely ignored the waking-up/getting-dressed scene.

Video_24 — Mixed
Short compilation video. Moment-DETR does better here (0.2529). A great hit:

"Additional parkour sequences" (1:54–2:19) → IoU 0.859
But 3 events get zero IoU from CG-DETR because the VLM descriptions all pointed to the 42–145s range, leaving the 9–96s region poorly covered.

