Summary Video Quality
The summary for video_23 is the worst affected — it selected 5 clips all from 144–186s (the last 40 seconds of a 3-minute video), missing the entire parkour run in the middle. This is directly traceable to the VLM failure on that video.

The summary for video_22 is the most sensible — it covers the parkour demonstrations from 0s to 230s in chronological order, which aligns well with what a human would pick.

Bottom Line
The pipeline works end-to-end and the IoU numbers (~0.24–0.28) are reasonable for a zero-shot pipeline with no fine-tuning. The biggest bottleneck is not the moment retrieval models — it is the VLM at Step 3. Garbage-in, garbage-out: if the VLM describes the wrong events or places them in the wrong temporal region, even a perfect moment retrieval model can't recover.